  "main_analytical_message": "Descriptive native-absorption share shifts +3.98 percentage points under a European evidence-filtered host link augmentation, more than the 0.36-point old-source conditional spatial null residual, but the two sensitivity contrasts are NOT equivalent and cannot establish the augmented spatial null.",
  "interpretation_ceiling": [
    "All introduced host × focal butterfly × region incidences are potential supply, not larvae, population or fitness observations.",
    "The BCE evidence comes from European records, is not a globally representative host inventory and should not be called an independent globally corrected dataset.",
    "WCVP extant distribution of a host plant anywhere does not confirm the butterfly feeds on it there; candidate European feeding relations are projected globally as an upper-bound sensitivity.",
    "The 158 unaffected butterflies retain the same native/introduced larval-resource candidate distributions and denominators.",
    "More host records may reclassify a formerly introduced-added resource cell into the native envelope.",
    "This augmented-source analysis is DESCRIPTIVE only. A new matched, numerically qualified spatial null would be needed to assess source-robustness of the old +271/+276 incidence residual.",
